      {
        "id": 239198,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-07-11T23:08:11.932Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\" data-post=\"22\" data-topic=\"28661\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>She’s a girl with <em>magical</em> control over all birds.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>True, but with the exception of one card in the Harpy’s deck, which is much later in her career after she explicitly starts learning Nightmist-style magic, all of what we see from her Matriarch phase gives no indication that she’s gating birds in from miles away; the power of the Mask seems only to send out a psychic call to all birds which are within flying distance to come fry to the wearer’s location.  This is admittedly not made clear at all, but in general my policy is to assume that a superpower/paranormal-phenomenon/etc. doesn’t exist unless it’s explicitly demonstrated to.  When all we see is a bunch of birds gathering around the Matriarch, my assumption is that they were already close by.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\" data-post=\"23\" data-topic=\"28661\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, there are turkey vultures in the Northeast.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Okay, I didn’t know that.  Is the one shown in the card actually a turkey vulture?</p>",
